From a1507d8a465a8003bb696af69d521d5b93c77233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:59:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/25] sglang DSA: record the IndexShare alternative at the
 point of use

Turning GLM-5.2 MTP IndexShare off avoids the same deadlock without patch 04 or
02's page-table half:

    --json-model-override-args '{"index_share_for_mtp_iteration":false}'

It works because IndexShare is the SOURCE of the divergence this set votes around:
the guard term dsa_topk_indices is None is seeded on the PD decode leg from
RDMA-shipped per-request payloads, so it is a function of which requests each rank
holds. No seed, no divergence.

Each diff now carries a header saying where it stands: 04 "ALTERNATIVE TO THIS
PATCH", 02 "PARTIAL ALTERNATIVE" (2b yes, 2a untested either way), 01 "NOT
substituted" (independent bug, present regardless). README gains the same as a
table plus the measurement.

Recorded honestly rather than as a recommendation: the arm that validated it ran
conc=64 not 128, needed prefill-leg MTP as well, and the override is nearly free
only while IndexShare's consumer stays disabled under PD by
should_use_dsa_fused_topk. Upstream #31477 removes that -- re-checked with gh
today: OPEN, REVIEW_REQUIRED, unmerged. Good answer today if IndexShare is not
wanted, dated one if it is.

The headers sit before the first "diff --git", which patch(1) skips. Verified by a
REAL --fuzz=0 apply into a pristine v0.5.15.post1 tree, in prerequisite order
(main's nextn script first): all three clean, 9 files modified. Not by --dry-run,
which fuzzes by default.

